\section{Frozen hypothesis and isolated change}
\textbf{Hypothesis.} \VAR{summary.hypothesis|latex}

Each arm predicts
\(\widehat y_h=y_{\mathrm{latest}}+(h/5)^\alpha\delta_\theta\).
The exponent is a fixed training and representation bias, not a fitted
physical law. It changes no parameter count. Architecture, weather features,
objective, raw uncertainty head, fold, seed, sample cap, and optimizer are
identical.

